    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890-a1">

                <pb facs="0923" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg835"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Tewfik Pasha to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte, Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1904-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                                1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Me. Envoy</hi>: In answer to the note that your
                    excellency addressed to me, dated the 26th of March last, No. 382, I have the
                    honor to inform you, according to a telegram of the governor-general of the
                    vilayet of Erzeroum, that categoric <pb facs="0924" n="836" xml:id="pg836"/>
                    orders have been given to the civil and military authorities for the arrest of
                    Seyid Ghaffar, accused of having assassinated the American missionary Labaree in
                    Persia, in the event of his passing into Ottoman territory.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tewfik.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
